Selenium Grid Configuration and Remote Execution
Aim: To configure Selenium Server using Hub-Node architecture and execute test scripts using RemoteWebDriver.

Software Requirements:
1. Eclipse IDE
2. Java JDK
3. Maven Project
4. Selenium Server 4.51.0
5. Google Chrome Browser
1. Procedure
1. Open Eclipse IDE.
2. Create a new Maven Project named SeleniumGrid.
3. Add Selenium dependency in the pom.xml file.
4. Update Maven Project to download Selenium libraries.
5. Download Selenium Server JAR file.
6. Start Selenium Hub using Command Prompt.
7. Start Selenium Node using another Command Prompt.
8. Open Selenium Grid Dashboard at http://localhost:4444.
9. Create a Java class named RemoteTest.
10. Write a program using RemoteWebDriver.
11. Execute the program and verify the browser result.
2. Maven Dependency (pom.xml)

<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">

    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.sql</groupId>
